    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a derived `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 `telephone` for humans (country code, space, national digits grouped in threes) while leaving raw `telephone` untouched.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`mapper/TelephoneDisplayResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 a static resolver (following the existing `LocalityResolver`/`CheckDigitResolver` pattern) that parses the E.164 value, detects the country code (known codes `61`, `1`, longest-first, mirroring `TelephoneNormalizer`), and groups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Falls back gracefully for null/blank/non-E.164 input and unknown country codes.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` calling the resolver from `owner.getTelephone()`.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (this is what generates the `OwnerDto` field the mapper targets).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes (`telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
